 "holdout": {
  "protocol": "Pre-registered external holdout benchmark (Milestone 28). Written before any holdout score was computed. Relevance comes only from BDD100K's own human labels: image tags (weather, timeofday, scene) and 2D boxes (area = box width*height as a fraction of the image). Fixed protocol: every method is run once, frozen, with no adjustment; metrics mAP and P@5; a query with fewer than 5 positives in the holdout is excluded on its label counts alone; families (a) condition, (b) object, (c) object x condition are reported separately and pooled; paired sign-flip tests vs SceneMiner. Main mode is metadata-free (no method reads BDD100K tags, which are the ground truth). A second, labelled-circular mode gives the methods that can read recorded metadata the BDD100K timeofday/weather tags as metadata. Queries a8-a10 use a weather/time tag as a proxy for a degradation BDD100K does not label.",
